module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.AmpleCluster.Basic
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.NonvanishingOpen.Basic
public import StacksFrontier.Topology.Sheaves.Glueing.OModuleMapGluing
public import Mathlib.AlgebraicGeometry.Morphisms.QuasiSeparated

/-!
# An invertible module on a quasi-affine scheme is generated by its global sections

The proof of Stacks Tag 0F20 quotes one result from elsewhere: on a quasi-affine scheme every
quasi-coherent `𝒪_X`-module is globally generated (Stacks Tags 01QE and 01Q3). Nothing of that
kind is in Mathlib at this pin -- `Mathlib/AlgebraicGeometry/QuasiAffine.lean` says nothing about
modules -- and nothing of it was in this repository. This file proves the case Tag 0F20 uses:
`L` invertible, generation read pointwise. It is the *only* input Tag 0F20 needs, and it is not
an artefact of the route: taking `E = {y}` and `W = ⊤` in Tag 0F20 returns exactly this
statement, so the two are equivalent.

## Main results

* `Stacks.QuasiAffineGlobalGeneration.exists_nonvanishing`: on a quasi-affine scheme `X`, for every
  invertible `𝒪_X`-module `L` and every `y : X`, some global section of `L` does not vanish at `y`.

## The proof

Write `A = Γ(X, 𝒪_X)`. A *chart* (`Stacks.QuasiAffineGlobalGeneration.Chart`) is a global function
`g : A` whose basic open `X_g` is affine and lies inside an open trivializing `L`; every point of a
quasi-affine scheme lies in one, by the prime avoidance lemma
`Stacks.AmpleCluster.exists_affine_basicOpen_of_finite_of_isQuasiAffine` applied inside a
trivializing open of the cover supplied by clause 2 of Stacks Tag 0B8M. Fix the point `y`, let
`f` cut out a chart around it and let `b` be the basis section of `L` on the trivializing open
of that chart. `X` is quasi-compact, so finitely many charts cover it, and the section wanted is
`f ^ j • b` extended over all of them:

1. **Extension** (`exists_pow_smul_res`). On a chart `U`, the overlap `U ⊓ X_f` is the basic open
   of `f|_U` in the *affine* `U`, so Mathlib's `exists_eq_pow_mul_of_isAffineOpen` clears a
   denominator: for every large enough `m` there is `a : Γ(L, U)` restricting to `f ^ m • b` on
   the overlap. The transition function enters as the trivializing function of `b` on the
   overlap, and `L` is free on `U`, so a section of `L` over `U` is a function times the chart's
   own basis section.
2. **Compatibility** (`exists_pow_smul_res_eq`). Two such extensions agree on the part of the
   overlap of their charts where `f` does not vanish, both being `f ^ m • b` there. The overlap
   of two charts is again affine -- it is a basic open of either of them -- and `L` is free on
   it, so the difference is a function vanishing on a basic open of an affine, hence killed by a
   power of `f` (`IsAffineOpen.isLocalization_basicOpen` and `IsLocalization.map_eq_zero_iff`).
3. **Gluing**. Taking the maximum of the finitely many exponents of step 1 and then of the
   finitely many exponents of step 2, the family becomes compatible on the nose and glues
   (`TopCat.Sheaf.existsUnique_gluing_of_isSheafPresheaf`).
4. **Nonvanishing** (`mem_nonvanishingLocus_of_res`). The glued section restricts near `y` to
   `f ^ j • b`; the germ of `f` at `y` is a unit because `y ∈ X_f`, and the germ of a basis
   section is never in `𝔪_y L_y`, so the germ of the glued section is not either.

No induction on a finite set, no reduced closed subscheme on a complement and no ideal sheaf of
a complement appear -- the source uses all three, for Tag 0F20 itself rather than for this input.

## Implementation notes

`Stacks.QuasiAffineGlobalGeneration.resL` and `Stacks.QuasiAffineGlobalGeneration.resO` are
Mathlib's `|_` with the inclusion passed explicitly rather than found by `restrict_tac`. They are
reducible, so they are interchangeable with `|_` for `exact`, but **not** for `rw`: `Γ(L, U)` is
`(Scheme.Modules.presheaf L).obj (op U)` and `Scheme.Modules.presheaf` is not reducible, so a `rw`
whose pattern is spelled one way and whose target is spelled the other fails with an application
type mismatch. Every such crossing below is therefore made by a `have` with an explicit type, which
is checked at default transparency; the same is why the glued section is re-obtained at the type
`Γ(L, ⊤)` before the last step, since the sheaf-condition lemma delivers it at `L.val.obj (op ⊤)`.

`Stacks.QuasiAffineGlobalGeneration.ov f U` is `X.basicOpen (f|_U)` and not `U ⊓ X_f`, although
`Stacks.QuasiAffineGlobalGeneration.ov_eq` says they are equal: stated the first way it is
literally the open that `exists_eq_pow_mul_of_isAffineOpen` and
`IsAffineOpen.isLocalization_basicOpen` speak about, so no section ever has to be transported along
an equality of opens.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0F20](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0F20)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01QE](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01QE)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01Q3](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01Q3)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0B8M](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0B8M)

## What is not done

Quasi-coherent modules in general are not treated: the argument uses local freeness of `L` at
three separate points (to name a transition function, to reduce the torsion step to the
structure sheaf, and to recognise a nonvanishing germ), and nothing here is stated for a module
that is merely quasi-coherent. No `stacks` attribute is attached in this file: Tags 01QE and
01Q3 are each a list of equivalent conditions, and this is one consequence of one of them, not a
covering set for either label.
-/

@[expose] public section

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory TopologicalSpace Opposite
open Stacks.Ample Stacks.ModuleStalk Stacks.NonvanishingOpen

universe u

namespace Stacks.QuasiAffineGlobalGeneration

variable {X : Scheme.{u}}

/-- **A chart for `L`**: an affine basic open `X_fn` of a global function, together with an open
`amb` containing it on which `L` is sectionwise trivialized. On a quasi-affine scheme the charts
cover `X` (`Stacks.QuasiAffineGlobalGeneration.exists_chart`), and the two properties are exactly
what the extension and compatibility steps consume -- affineness for the localization lemmas,
triviality to turn a section of `L` into a function. -/
structure Chart (X : Scheme.{u}) (L : X.Modules) where
  /-- The global function whose basic open is the chart. -/
  fn : Γ(X, ⊤)
  /-- An open containing the chart on which `L` is trivialized. -/
  amb : X.Opens
  /-- The sectionwise trivialization of `L` over `amb`. -/
  tv : Stacks.SheafDescent.Trivialization X.presheaf L.val amb
  /-- The chart is an affine open. -/
  isAffine : IsAffineOpen (X.basicOpen fn)
  /-- The chart is contained in the trivializing open. -/
  le : X.basicOpen fn ≤ amb

namespace Chart

variable {L : X.Modules}

/-- The chart itself, as an open subset of `X`. -/
abbrev dom (c : Chart X L) : X.Opens := X.basicOpen c.fn

end Chart

/-- **Every point of a quasi-affine scheme lies in a chart.** Clause 2 of Stacks Tag 0B8M gives
an open cover trivializing `L`, and prime avoidance in `Γ(X, 𝒪_X)` shrinks a member of it to an
affine basic open of a global function around the given point. -/
theorem exists_chart [X.IsQuasiAffine] (L : X.Modules) [IsInvertibleModule X L] (x : X) :
    ∃ c : Chart X L, x ∈ c.dom := by
  obtain ⟨V, hV, htriv⟩ := Stacks.SheafRankOne.exists_cover_trivialization_of_isInvertible
    (X := X.toRingedSpace) X.ringCatSheaf.2 L
  obtain ⟨z, hz⟩ : ∃ z : X, x ∈ V z := Opens.mem_iSup.mp (hV ▸ Opens.mem_top x)
  obtain ⟨t⟩ := htriv z
  obtain ⟨g, haff, hxg, hgV⟩ :=
    Stacks.AmpleCluster.exists_affine_basicOpen_of_finite_of_isQuasiAffine
      (Set.finite_singleton x) (V z) (Set.singleton_subset_iff.mpr hz)
  exact ⟨⟨g, V z, t, haff, hgV⟩, hxg rfl⟩

/-! ### Restriction, with the inclusion given explicitly -/

/-- Restriction of a section of an `𝒪_X`-module along an inclusion of opens. -/
noncomputable abbrev resL {L : X.Modules} {V W : X.Opens} (h : W ≤ V) (s : Γ(L, V)) : Γ(L, W) :=
  L.presheaf.map (homOfLE h).op s

/-- Restriction of a section of the structure sheaf along an inclusion of opens. -/
abbrev resO {V W : X.Opens} (h : W ≤ V) (a : Γ(X, V)) : Γ(X, W) :=
  X.presheaf.map (homOfLE h).op a

/-- Restricting a section of a module twice is restricting once. -/
theorem resL_resL {L : X.Modules} {V W Z : X.Opens} (h : W ≤ V) (h' : Z ≤ W) (s : Γ(L, V)) :
    resL h' (resL h s) = resL (h'.trans h) s :=
  TopCat.Presheaf.restrict_restrict h' h s

/-- Restricting a section of the structure sheaf twice is restricting once. -/
theorem resO_resO {V W Z : X.Opens} (h : W ≤ V) (h' : Z ≤ W) (a : Γ(X, V)) :
    resO h' (resO h a) = resO (h'.trans h) a :=
  TopCat.Presheaf.restrict_restrict h' h a

/-- Restriction of sections is semilinear along restriction of functions. -/
theorem resL_smul {L : X.Modules} {V W : X.Opens} (h : W ≤ V) (a : Γ(X, V)) (s : Γ(L, V)) :
    resL h (a • s) = resO h a • resL h s :=
  Scheme.Modules.map_smul L (homOfLE h) a s

/-- Restriction of functions is multiplicative. -/
theorem resO_mul {V W : X.Opens} (h : W ≤ V) (a b : Γ(X, V)) :
    resO h (a * b) = resO h a * resO h b := by simp

/-- Restriction of functions commutes with powers. -/
theorem resO_pow {V W : X.Opens} (h : W ≤ V) (a : Γ(X, V)) (n : ℕ) :
    resO h (a ^ n) = resO h a ^ n := by
  simp

/-! ### The part of an open where a global function does not vanish -/

/-- The part of the open `U` on which the global function `f` does not vanish, spelled as the
basic open of the restriction of `f`, which is the shape `exists_eq_pow_mul_of_isAffineOpen`
consumes. -/
abbrev ov (f : Γ(X, ⊤)) (U : X.Opens) : X.Opens := X.basicOpen (resO (le_top : U ≤ ⊤) f)

/-- The nonvanishing part of an open lies in that open. -/
theorem ov_le (f : Γ(X, ⊤)) (U : X.Opens) : ov f U ≤ U := X.basicOpen_le _

/-- The nonvanishing part of `U` is `U ⊓ X_f`. -/
theorem ov_eq (f : Γ(X, ⊤)) (U : X.Opens) : ov f U = U ⊓ X.basicOpen f := by
  rw [ov, Scheme.basicOpen_res]

/-- The nonvanishing part of an open lies in `X_f`. -/
theorem ov_le_basicOpen (f : Γ(X, ⊤)) (U : X.Opens) : ov f U ≤ X.basicOpen f := by
  rw [ov_eq]; exact inf_le_right

/-- An open inside both `U` and `X_f` lies in the nonvanishing part of `U`. -/
theorem le_ov (f : Γ(X, ⊤)) {U Z : X.Opens} (h : Z ≤ U) (h' : Z ≤ X.basicOpen f) :
    Z ≤ ov f U := by
  rw [ov_eq]; exact le_inf h h'

/-! ### The trivialization, two missing pieces -/

/-- A trivializing map is injective on sections: it is an isomorphism. -/
theorem triv_inj {L : X.Modules} {V : X.Opens}
    (t : Stacks.SheafDescent.Trivialization X.presheaf L.val V) {W : X.Opens} (h : W ⟶ V) :
    Function.Injective (NonvanishingOpen.triv t h) := (t.θ W h).injective

/-- A trivializing map sends the zero section to `0`. -/
theorem triv_zero {L : X.Modules} {V : X.Opens}
    (t : Stacks.SheafDescent.Trivialization X.presheaf L.val V) {W : X.Opens} (h : W ⟶ V) :
    NonvanishingOpen.triv t h 0 = 0 := (t.θ W h).map_zero

/-- The trivializing function commutes with restriction, with the inclusions given explicitly. -/
theorem triv_resO {L : X.Modules} {V : X.Opens}
    (t : Stacks.SheafDescent.Trivialization X.presheaf L.val V) {W W' : X.Opens} (h : W ≤ V)
    (h' : W' ≤ W) (u : Γ(L, W)) :
    NonvanishingOpen.triv t (homOfLE (h'.trans h)) (resL h' u)
      = resO h' (NonvanishingOpen.triv t (homOfLE h) u) :=
  NonvanishingOpen.triv_res t (homOfLE h) (homOfLE h') (homOfLE (h'.trans h)) u

/-- On an open inside a trivializing open, a section is its trivializing function times the
restricted basis section. -/
theorem eq_triv_smul_basis_res {L : X.Modules} {V : X.Opens}
    (t : Stacks.SheafDescent.Trivialization X.presheaf L.val V) {W : X.Opens} (h : W ≤ V)
    (u : Γ(L, W)) :
    u = NonvanishingOpen.triv t (homOfLE h) u • resL h (NonvanishingOpen.basis t) := by
  refine triv_inj t (homOfLE h) ?_
  rw [NonvanishingOpen.triv_smul, NonvanishingOpen.triv_res_basis t (homOfLE h), mul_one]

/-! ### Clearing the denominator on one chart -/

/-- **The extension step.** Given a global function `f`, a section `b` of `L` over an open
containing `X_f`, and a chart `c`, some multiple `f ^ m • b` of `b` extends from the overlap
`ov f c.dom` to the whole chart, and this holds for every large enough `m`. -/
theorem exists_pow_smul_res (L : X.Modules) (f : Γ(X, ⊤)) {V₀ : X.Opens}
    (hV₀ : X.basicOpen f ≤ V₀) (b : Γ(L, V₀)) (c : Chart X L) :
    ∃ n : ℕ, ∀ m : ℕ, n ≤ m → ∃ a : Γ(L, c.dom),
      resL (ov_le f c.dom) a =
        resO (le_top : ov f c.dom ≤ ⊤) f ^ m • resL ((ov_le_basicOpen f c.dom).trans hV₀) b := by
  obtain ⟨n, d, hd⟩ := exists_eq_pow_mul_of_isAffineOpen X c.dom c.isAffine
    (resO (le_top : c.dom ≤ ⊤) f) (NonvanishingOpen.triv c.tv
      (homOfLE ((ov_le f c.dom).trans c.le)) (resL ((ov_le_basicOpen f c.dom).trans hV₀) b))
  have hd' : resO (ov_le f c.dom) d =
      resO (le_top : ov f c.dom ≤ ⊤) f ^ n *
        NonvanishingOpen.triv c.tv (homOfLE ((ov_le f c.dom).trans c.le))
          (resL ((ov_le_basicOpen f c.dom).trans hV₀) b) := by
    rw [← resO_resO (le_top : c.dom ≤ ⊤) (ov_le f c.dom) f]
    exact hd
  refine ⟨n, fun m hm => ⟨(resO (le_top : c.dom ≤ ⊤) f ^ (m - n) * d) • resL c.le
    (NonvanishingOpen.basis c.tv), ?_⟩⟩
  rw [resL_smul, resL_resL, resO_mul, resO_pow, resO_resO, hd', ← mul_assoc, ← pow_add,
    Nat.sub_add_cancel hm, mul_smul]
  congr 1
  exact (eq_triv_smul_basis_res c.tv ((ov_le f c.dom).trans c.le) _).symm

/-- Restriction of sections is additive. -/
theorem resL_sub {L : X.Modules} {V W : X.Opens} (h : W ≤ V) (s t : Γ(L, V)) :
    resL h (s - t) = resL h s - resL h t := by
  simp

/-- Two charts overlap in an affine open: the overlap is a basic open of either chart. -/
theorem isAffineOpen_inf (L : X.Modules) (c₁ c₂ : Chart X L) :
    IsAffineOpen (c₁.dom ⊓ c₂.dom) := by
  have hZeq : X.basicOpen (resO (le_top : c₁.dom ≤ ⊤) c₂.fn) = c₁.dom ⊓ c₂.dom := by
    rw [Scheme.basicOpen_res]
  exact hZeq ▸ c₁.isAffine.basicOpen _

/-- **The compatibility step.** Two extensions produced by `exists_pow_smul_res` at the same
exponent agree on the overlap of their charts after multiplication by a large enough power of
`f`: they already agree where `f` does not vanish, and the overlap is affine, so the difference
is killed by a power of `f`. -/
theorem exists_pow_smul_res_eq (L : X.Modules) (f : Γ(X, ⊤)) {V₀ : X.Opens}
    (hV₀ : X.basicOpen f ≤ V₀) (b : Γ(L, V₀)) (c₁ c₂ : Chart X L) {n : ℕ}
    {a₁ : Γ(L, c₁.dom)} {a₂ : Γ(L, c₂.dom)}
    (h₁ : resL (ov_le f c₁.dom) a₁ =
      resO (le_top : ov f c₁.dom ≤ ⊤) f ^ n • resL ((ov_le_basicOpen f c₁.dom).trans hV₀) b)
    (h₂ : resL (ov_le f c₂.dom) a₂ =
      resO (le_top : ov f c₂.dom ≤ ⊤) f ^ n • resL ((ov_le_basicOpen f c₂.dom).trans hV₀) b) :
    ∃ k : ℕ, ∀ m : ℕ, k ≤ m →
      resO (le_top : c₁.dom ⊓ c₂.dom ≤ ⊤) f ^ m •
          resL (inf_le_left : c₁.dom ⊓ c₂.dom ≤ c₁.dom) a₁ =
        resO (le_top : c₁.dom ⊓ c₂.dom ≤ ⊤) f ^ m •
          resL (inf_le_right : c₁.dom ⊓ c₂.dom ≤ c₂.dom) a₂ := by
  have e : ∀ {U W : X.Opens} (hW : W ≤ U) (a : Γ(L, U)),
      resL (ov_le f U) a =
        resO (le_top : ov f U ≤ ⊤) f ^ n • resL ((ov_le_basicOpen f U).trans hV₀) b →
      resL (ov_le f W) (resL hW a) =
        resO (le_top : ov f W ≤ ⊤) f ^ n • resL ((ov_le_basicOpen f W).trans hV₀) b := by
    intro U W hW a h
    rw [resL_resL, ← resL_resL (ov_le f U) (le_ov f ((ov_le f W).trans hW) (ov_le_basicOpen f W)),
      h, resL_smul, resO_pow, resO_resO, resL_resL]
  have e₁ := e (inf_le_left : c₁.dom ⊓ c₂.dom ≤ c₁.dom) a₁ h₁
  have e₂ := e (inf_le_right : c₁.dom ⊓ c₂.dom ≤ c₂.dom) a₂ h₂
  have hδ : resL (ov_le f (c₁.dom ⊓ c₂.dom))
      (resL (inf_le_left : c₁.dom ⊓ c₂.dom ≤ c₁.dom) a₁ -
        resL (inf_le_right : c₁.dom ⊓ c₂.dom ≤ c₂.dom) a₂) = 0 := by
    rw [resL_sub, e₁, e₂, sub_self]
  have hg : resO (ov_le f (c₁.dom ⊓ c₂.dom))
      (NonvanishingOpen.triv c₁.tv (homOfLE (inf_le_left.trans c₁.le))
        (resL (inf_le_left : c₁.dom ⊓ c₂.dom ≤ c₁.dom) a₁ -
          resL (inf_le_right : c₁.dom ⊓ c₂.dom ≤ c₂.dom) a₂)) = 0 := by
    rw [← triv_resO c₁.tv (inf_le_left.trans c₁.le) (ov_le f (c₁.dom ⊓ c₂.dom)), hδ, triv_zero]
  have hloc := (isAffineOpen_inf L c₁ c₂).isLocalization_basicOpen
    (resO (le_top : c₁.dom ⊓ c₂.dom ≤ ⊤) f)
  have hg' : algebraMap Γ(X, c₁.dom ⊓ c₂.dom) Γ(X, ov f (c₁.dom ⊓ c₂.dom))
      (NonvanishingOpen.triv c₁.tv (homOfLE (inf_le_left.trans c₁.le))
        (resL (inf_le_left : c₁.dom ⊓ c₂.dom ≤ c₁.dom) a₁ -
          resL (inf_le_right : c₁.dom ⊓ c₂.dom ≤ c₂.dom) a₂)) = 0 := hg
  obtain ⟨u, hu⟩ := (IsLocalization.map_eq_zero_iff
    (Submonoid.powers (resO (le_top : c₁.dom ⊓ c₂.dom ≤ ⊤) f))
    Γ(X, ov f (c₁.dom ⊓ c₂.dom)) _).mp hg'
  obtain ⟨k, hk⟩ := u.2
  rw [← hk] at hu
  refine ⟨k, fun m hm => ?_⟩
  have hzero : resO (le_top : c₁.dom ⊓ c₂.dom ≤ ⊤) f ^ m •
      (resL (inf_le_left : c₁.dom ⊓ c₂.dom ≤ c₁.dom) a₁ -
        resL (inf_le_right : c₁.dom ⊓ c₂.dom ≤ c₂.dom) a₂) = 0 := by
    refine triv_inj c₁.tv (homOfLE (inf_le_left.trans c₁.le)) ?_
    rw [NonvanishingOpen.triv_smul, triv_zero, ← Nat.sub_add_cancel hm, pow_add, mul_assoc, hu,
      mul_zero]
  rw [smul_sub, sub_eq_zero] at hzero
  exact hzero

/-- The restriction map of the sheaf-condition API is the restriction map used here. -/
theorem resLE_eq {L : X.Modules} {V W : X.Opens} (h : W ≤ V) (s : Γ(L, V)) :
    PresheafOfModules.resLE L.val h s = resL h s := rfl

/-! ### Global generation -/

/-- **The nonvanishing test.** A global section that restricts, on the part of an open where the
global function `f` does not vanish, to a power of `f` times a basis section of a trivialization,
does not vanish at any point of that part. -/
theorem mem_nonvanishingLocus_of_res (L : X.Modules) (f : Γ(X, ⊤)) {V₀ : X.Opens}
    (hV₀ : X.basicOpen f ≤ V₀) (t : Stacks.SheafDescent.Trivialization X.presheaf L.val V₀)
    {U : X.Opens} {y : X} (hy : y ∈ ov f U) (j : ℕ) (s : Γ(L, ⊤))
    (hs : resL (le_top : ov f U ≤ ⊤) s =
      resO (le_top : ov f U ≤ ⊤) f ^ j •
        resL ((ov_le_basicOpen f U).trans hV₀) (NonvanishingOpen.basis t)) :
    y ∈ nonvanishingLocus L s := by
  have key : (L.presheaf.Γgerm y).hom s =
      (L.presheaf.germ (ov f U) y hy).hom (resL (le_top : ov f U ≤ ⊤) s) :=
    (TopCat.Presheaf.Γgerm_res_apply (i := homOfLE (le_top : ov f U ≤ ⊤)) L.presheaf y hy s).symm
  have hgf : (X.presheaf.germ (ov f U) y hy).hom (resO (le_top : ov f U ≤ ⊤) f) =
      (X.presheaf.Γgerm y).hom f :=
    TopCat.Presheaf.germ_res_apply X.presheaf (homOfLE (le_top : ov f U ≤ ⊤)) y hy f
  have hgb : (L.presheaf.germ (ov f U) y hy).hom
        (resL ((ov_le_basicOpen f U).trans hV₀) (NonvanishingOpen.basis t)) =
      (L.presheaf.germ V₀ y (hV₀ (ov_le_basicOpen f U hy))).hom (NonvanishingOpen.basis t) :=
    TopCat.Presheaf.germ_res_apply L.presheaf
      (homOfLE ((ov_le_basicOpen f U).trans hV₀)) y hy (NonvanishingOpen.basis t)
  rw [mem_nonvanishingLocus_iff, key, hs, germ_smul, map_pow, hgf, hgb,
    smul_mem_maximalSmul_iff, not_or, not_not]
  exact ⟨IsUnit.pow _ ((X.mem_basicOpen_top f y).mp (ov_le_basicOpen f U hy)),
    NonvanishingOpen.notMem_maximalSmul_germ_basis t (hV₀ (ov_le_basicOpen f U hy))⟩

/-- **An invertible module on a quasi-affine scheme is generated by its global sections.**
At every point some global section of `L` fails to vanish. This is the invertible case of the
statement "on a quasi-affine scheme every quasi-coherent module is globally generated" that the
proof of Stacks Tag 0F20 quotes from Stacks Tags 01QE and 01Q3, and it is the only input that
Tag 0F20 needs. -/
theorem exists_nonvanishing [X.IsQuasiAffine] (L : X.Modules) [IsInvertibleModule X L] (y : X) :
    ∃ s : Γ(L, ⊤), y ∈ nonvanishingLocus L s := by
  classical
  choose c hc using exists_chart L
  obtain ⟨t, ht⟩ := isCompact_univ.elim_finite_subcover (fun x : X => ((c x).dom : Set X))
    (fun x => (c x).dom.2) fun x _ => Set.mem_iUnion.mpr ⟨x, hc x⟩
  have hcov : (⊤ : X.Opens) ≤ ⨆ i : {x // x ∈ insert y t}, (c i.1).dom := by
    intro x _
    obtain ⟨x', hx', hxx'⟩ := Set.mem_iUnion₂.mp (ht (Set.mem_univ x))
    exact Opens.mem_iSup.mpr ⟨⟨x', Finset.mem_insert_of_mem hx'⟩, hxx'⟩
  choose n hn using fun i : {x // x ∈ insert y t} =>
    exists_pow_smul_res L (c y).fn (c y).le (NonvanishingOpen.basis (c y).tv) (c i.1)
  set N := Finset.univ.sup n with hNdef
  choose a ha using fun i => hn i N (Finset.le_sup (Finset.mem_univ i))
  choose k hk using fun p : {x // x ∈ insert y t} × {x // x ∈ insert y t} =>
    exists_pow_smul_res_eq L (c y).fn (c y).le (NonvanishingOpen.basis (c y).tv)
      (c p.1.1) (c p.2.1) (ha p.1) (ha p.2)
  set K := Finset.univ.sup k with hKdef
  have hcompat : ∀ i j : {x // x ∈ insert y t},
      PresheafOfModules.resLE L.val (inf_le_left : (c i.1).dom ⊓ (c j.1).dom ≤ (c i.1).dom)
          (resO (le_top : (c i.1).dom ≤ ⊤) (c y).fn ^ K • a i) =
        PresheafOfModules.resLE L.val (inf_le_right : (c i.1).dom ⊓ (c j.1).dom ≤ (c j.1).dom)
          (resO (le_top : (c j.1).dom ≤ ⊤) (c y).fn ^ K • a j) := by
    intro i j
    rw [resLE_eq, resLE_eq, resL_smul, resL_smul, resO_pow, resO_pow, resO_resO, resO_resO]
    exact hk (i, j) K (Finset.le_sup (Finset.mem_univ (i, j)))
  obtain ⟨σ₀, hσ₀, -⟩ := TopCat.Sheaf.existsUnique_gluing_of_isSheafPresheaf L.isSheaf
    (fun i : {x // x ∈ insert y t} => (c i.1).dom) (fun _ => le_top) hcov
    (fun i => resO (le_top : (c i.1).dom ≤ ⊤) (c y).fn ^ K • a i) hcompat
  obtain ⟨σ, hσ⟩ : ∃ σ : Γ(L, ⊤), ∀ i : {x // x ∈ insert y t},
      resL (le_top : (c i.1).dom ≤ ⊤) σ =
        resO (le_top : (c i.1).dom ≤ ⊤) (c y).fn ^ K • a i := ⟨σ₀, hσ₀⟩
  have hyP : y ∈ ov (c y).fn (c y).dom := by rw [ov_eq]; exact ⟨hc y, hc y⟩
  refine ⟨σ, mem_nonvanishingLocus_of_res L (c y).fn (c y).le (c y).tv hyP (K + N) σ ?_⟩
  rw [← resL_resL (le_top : (c y).dom ≤ ⊤) (ov_le (c y).fn (c y).dom),
    hσ ⟨y, Finset.mem_insert_self y t⟩, resL_smul, resO_pow, resO_resO,
    ha ⟨y, Finset.mem_insert_self y t⟩, smul_smul, ← pow_add]

end Stacks.QuasiAffineGlobalGeneration

